{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":425851,"duration_api_ms":381911,"ttft_ms":2299,"num_turns":26,"result":"## Summary\n\nI translated the C project at `c_src/` to Rust with byte-identical output.\n\n### Project structure\n- **`Cargo.toml`** — declares both a `[lib]` (`crate-type = [\"cdylib\", \"rlib\"]`) and a `[[bin]]` named `driver`. Cargo features mirror the CMake cache variables in lowercase:\n  - `OP` → features `add`, `sub`, `mul`\n  - `REPEAT` → features `repeat_0`..`repeat_7`\n  - Default features: `add`, `repeat_5` (matches `CMakeLists.txt` defaults).\n- **`src/lib.rs`** — translates `mdcore.c` plus the `mdmacros.h` macro machinery. Compile-time `cfg(feature = \"...\")` selects the OP step function / init / OP_FN, and a const `REPEAT` integer. All public C-visible functions (`op_add`, `op_sub`, `op_mul`, `helper_call`, `helper_ptr`, `use_generated`) and globals (`G_OP`, `G_OP_NAME`) are exported with `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"` and use `c_int`/`c_char` types.\n- **`src/main.rs`** — translates `mdmain.c`. Re-implements `atoi` semantics (whitespace, optional sign, decimal digits, wrapping overflow) so argument parsing matches the C version, and prints the same lines in the same order using `println!`.\n\n### Verification\nAll 24 combinations of `OP × REPEAT` were tested by building the C version with CMake and comparing stdout against the Rust binary built with matching features — every combination produced byte-identical output. Various integer inputs (positive, negative, zero, large) also matched.\n\nBoth `target/release/driver` (binary) and `target/release/libdriver.so` (cdylib) build cleanly.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a849b8ab-d7d2-4191-9e32-7f4a766a8431","total_cost_usd":1.25096325,"usage":{"input_tokens":30,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22041,"cache_read_input_tokens":613164,"output_tokens":32259,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tie